{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And Balaam rose up in the morning.</b> Perhaps because it was bad news for them, he did not wish to reveal it to them at night, for as we have said they were lodged in his own inn, and he waited until morning. Or it may intend that he did not rise from his sleep until morning, and that is the verse's saying <b>and Balaam rose up in the morning</b> — and not earlier. Or it is possible that Scripture speaks in disparagement of Balaam, that he sent them off quickly so that he could quickly send after other, more distinguished men. Or to make known his narrowness of eye, that he hastened to send them off before the time for eating arrived — the opposite of the generosity of the father of the girl, the concubine at Gibeah (Judges 19), who said to his son-in-law who arose to leave in the morning: ״סְעָד לִבְּךָ פַּת לֶחֶם וְאַחַר תֵּלֵכוּ״ — for this wicked man is the source of narrowness of eye, and he rose in the morning to send them off and told them to go to their land, because he feared they would linger in the city and their meal would be on him." "<b>Go, etc., for HaShem refuses, etc.</b> He suppressed half the matter and did not tell them anything except the first statement that HaShem had said to him — <b>you shall not go with them</b> — on account of their lowly status; and he did not tell them the statement <b>you shall not curse</b>, etc., for because of this Balak turned back and sent many distinguished men. Or perhaps that wicked man reasoned from the words of HaShem, for He gave the reason ״כִּי בָרוּךְ הוּא״, which comes to imply that at a time when He is not blessed he may curse him; therefore he did not give them a definitive answer until he would send those fit to go with them — perhaps the time would then be one in which He would not be blessed."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:12:28.124956172Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}